WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.200
Narrator: A little more than
a week after the release

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.030
of "Avengers: Endgame," we are
treated to an all-new trailer

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:09.890
for "Spider-Man: Far From Home,"

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.160
and if you thought it was going to be

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.370
a quaint little movie, think again.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.139
I'm talking about a multiverse.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.800
Here's everything you might've missed

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.720
in the new "Spider-Man" trailer.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.600
It starts with a spoiler
warning from actor Tom Holland.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.230
He says if you haven't seen "Endgame,"

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.690
then don't watch the trailer.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:26.640
We'll say the same.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.390
The trailer starts with Peter Parker

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.970
talking to Happy Hogan.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.720
He says he misses Iron Man.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.640
Iron Man, of course, died in "Endgame"

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.730
when he snapped the
custom Infinity Gauntlet,

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.210
wiping Thanos and his
armies from the universe.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.930
It seems that the whole world now knows

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:45.030
about Iron Man's sacrifice,
as Tony Stark is memorialized

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.810
in street art throughout the trailer

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.850
and what appears to be art-class drawings

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.630
in the background of this shot.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:53.060
Happy tells Peter that
Tony sacrificed himself

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.320
because he knew Spider-Man
would be around.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.360
This seems likely.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.100
In "Endgame," Tony spots
this photo of him and Peter

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.030
before deciding to take a
stab at solving time travel

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.960
to reverse the Thanos snap.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.060
Then, we cut to Peter
Parker fighting some goons

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.220
in his Iron Spider suit that Tony gave him

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.490
in "Avengers: Infinity War."

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:12.560
Peter: And this suit is
ridiculously intuitive, by the way.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.040
Narrator: After Spider-Man
takes care of the goons,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.320
a police officer asks
him if he's going to be

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.540
the next Iron Man.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.700
This question seems like an important one.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:22.140
Peter appears reluctant
to take on this burden.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.050
Peter: Well, no, I don't have time.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:24.419
I'm too busy doing your jobs.

00:01:24.419 --> 00:01:25.252
Cops: Oh! What?

00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:26.410
Narrator: Later in the trailer, he says,

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.510
"I'm just a friendly
neighborhood Spider-Man,"

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.950
but then, towards the end of
the trailer, Peter says...

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.890
The world needs the next Iron Man.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.120
Narrator: And in the last trailer,

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.420
one of Peter's classmates says Mysterio

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.140
is like Iron Man and
Thor all rolled into one.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.930
Seems like everyone is
trying to figure out

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.660
who can replace Tony Stark.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.210
Spider-Man tells the cops
he's going on vacation.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.510
We knew from the last trailer

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.070
that Spider-Man and his classmates

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:49.600
were going on a trip to Europe,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.460
but turns out "Far From
Home" might take Peter

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.040
a lot further than just across the pond.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.860
More on that in a bit.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.480
Speaking of Peter's classmates,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.460
a big question at the end of "Endgame" is,

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.330
who exactly from Peter's
high school got snapped away

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.830
for five years after Thanos' first snap?

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.370
It seems like the whole class

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.370
is still in high school five years later,

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:12.350
which suggests that they might've
missed out on those years

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.200
because Thanos snapped them all away,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.730
but statistically, this
seems highly unlikely.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.150
Hopefully, we'll get an answer
when the movie comes out.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.930
Next, Happy and Peter have
a comical conversation.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.360
Nick Fury tries to call Peter,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.250
but Peter sends him straight to voicemail.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.420
Nick and Peter probably
would've met at Tony's funeral

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.450
at the end of "Endgame."

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.100
Happy: You do not ghost Nick Fury!

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.080
Narrator: Notice the
Crusher Hogan fight sign

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.230
in the background of this scene.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.720
This is a character in the
comics that Spider-Man fights

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.060
when he wants to test
out his brand-new powers.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.590
We first see Crusher in the comics

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.360
in "Amazing Fantasy" No. 15.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.620
Nick Fury finally gets
in contact with Peter,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.600
meeting him in Europe,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.340
but we knew that from the last trailer.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.910
What we didn't know is that
Fury introduces Spider-Man

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.330
to Mr. Beck, or Quentin
Beck in the comics,

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.610
also known as Mysterio, and
here's where the magic happens.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.150
Fury explains...

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.940
Nick: Beck is from Earth, just not ours.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.740
Peter: You're saying there's a multiverse?

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.810
Narrator: There are an
unlimited number of Earths

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.260
in Marvel, which allows
for multiple possibilities.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.870
Earth 616 is the main
universe from the comics,

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.660
while the MCU is referred
to as Earth 199,999.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.900
Our Earth is designated Earth 1218,

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.510
and superheroes don't exist on it.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.360
A multiverse opens up the possibilities

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.450
for stories like Peggy
Carter being injected

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.380
with Super Soldier Serum
and teams like the Exiles.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.700
The Exiles are heroes,

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.410
all selected from different dimensions,

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.740
who hop around the multiverse,
trying to fix things

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.090
that may have gone bad on various Earths.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.680
Fury also tells Peter
that the snap tore a hole

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.160
in our dimension, which begs
the question, which snap?

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.820
We've seen four Infinity
Stone snaps so far.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.420
The first was in "Infinity War,"

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.080
which wiped out half of life.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.627
Then in "Endgame," Thanos
snapped again to destroy the

00:03:44.627 --> 00:03:45.460
stones. After the Avengers retrieve

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:46.293
the stones from the past,

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:50.340
the Hulk snaps to bring
everyone who disappeared back.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.640
Then Tony snapped a fourth time

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.520
to rid the universe of Thanos.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.290
The trailer conveniently gives us a reason

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.220
why Spider-Man is Fury's best hope.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.720
Apparently, Thor is off-world

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.290
and Captain Marvel is simply...

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:01.123
Maria: Unavailable.

00:04:01.123 --> 00:04:02.860
Narrator: Oh, hey, it's Agent Maria Hill.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:04.450
We haven't seen her since
she was snapped away

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.400
by Thanos in "Infinity War."

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.510
Next up, the dry-humored
MJ has figured out

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.000
that Peter is Spider-Man,

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.970
which is sure to have a big
impact on their relationship.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.820
In the Sam Raimi "Spider-Man" series,

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.590
when Mary Jane learned
Peter was Spider-Man,

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:19.050
things didn't end well, but
that was "Spider-Man 3,"

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.090
and we do not talk about "Spider-Man 3."

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.820
MJ here isn't Mary Jane,
but her knowing his secret

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.060
could still spell trouble.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.810
MJ: I mean, it's kind of obvious.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.960
Narrator: If Mysterio is
from another dimension,

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.590
it makes sense that the group of villains

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.580
that they appear to be
fighting are The Elementals,

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.150
four extra-dimensional
villains who each control

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:38.940
different elements: fire,
water, earth, and air.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.500
But Mysterio in the comics
is the master of illusions,

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.230
and he's a total bad guy,
so it could be possible

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.320
that everything is an illusion
meant to make Mysterio

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.900
look like the hero in the absence

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.420
of one of Earth's
greatest heroes, Iron Man.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.030
In the comics, Mysterio frames
Spider-Man as a criminal

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.390
using his powers of illusion.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.240
Mysterio then tried to make himself

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.400
look like a hero by capturing Spidey.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.120
We see Peter wearing these glasses,

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.000
which look an awful lot
like the glasses Tony wore.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.900
When he takes them off,
Peter looks shocked.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.700
These glasses could be a
filter that allow him to see

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.100
that there's no attack at all

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.407
and it's all an illusion
created by Mysterio.

00:05:12.407 --> 00:05:13.380
Peter: Oh, my God.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.730
Narrator: So what'd you
think of the trailer?

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.210
Are you excited for "Far From Home"?

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.883
Let us know in the comments.

